[Music]  while plenty of games have a level  creator mode of some type Nintendo Super  Mario maker for Wii U takes that idea to  a whole new level the entire game is  built around creating and sharing your  own 2d Mario stages and with a seamless  intuitive design Mario maker can help  even the most talent 'less creators like  me feel like they could be an actual  designer in the Creator part of Mario  maker you crib elements from several  Mario games and toss them together into  a level of your own making that you then  upload online for everyone else to play  you choose the overall graphical skin  from among several classical Mario games  which affects the way everything looks  sounds and some of the available items  for example the cape feather and Mario  world is swapped out for the propeller  and new super mario brothers you and the  background that you choose airship  underwater a castle etc determines the  stage and musical themes the  mix-and-match nature allows for  anachronistic additions to familiar  scenes like a giant Koopa with a cannon  firing Chain Chomp strapped to its back  [Music]  it's a simple drag-and-drop system and  the hand representing your on-screen  stylus can be swapped to represent  lefties righties different skin tones or  even a cat paw and creating scenery and  platforms is as easy as dragging your  stylus across the level as you place two  obstacles and platforms little  background elements pop up adding color  and variety you can even drop in  pre-recorded sound and visual effects to  your stages like a beating heart to add  some tension to an ominous dungeon  hallway and with an undo dog button and  a restart rocket icon the menu aesthetic  is an obvious nod to the quirky  experimental SNES title Mario Paint  everything is incredibly easy to  understand to implement and experiment  with which makes creating levels even  for a complete novice fun and effortless  experimenting with the creation tools  and playing around with the maker aspect  is fun on its own but you really learn  to use those tools through trying out  levels Mario maker comes with a suite of  pre-built stages but the user created  levels are where the real genius and  maddening difficulty come in the game  makes it easy to find and sort user  created levels by popularity difficulty  and creator  but the force that keeps driving you  through these player-created levels no  matter how crazy is knowing that someone  had to beat them to upload them they  might seem unbelievably unfair but  someone beat that level at least once  and that means you can too and those  broad strokes don't even go into things  like the music from the familiar themes  of the main world's to the altered riffs  you get when tinkering around in make  mode the soundtrack captures the same  essence of Wonder and surprise as the  rest of the game even the in-game  instruction manual is incredibly useful  and entertaining  it's graphically animated written with a  great sense of humor and for no  particular reason throws in some  thoughts about Brussels sprouts Super  Mario maker is a game of joyous creation  and fun surprises and for the first time  in a creation focus game I look forward  to returning again and again not just  for the amazing levels I know other  people will create but to keep trying to  make my own levels better the game won't  necessarily turn you into the next  Shigeru Miyamoto but you can almost feel  a little bit of that magic rubbing off  every time you upload a new creation  [Music]  [Music]

